{:edb/db-before-t 1469 :edb/db-after-t 1470 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534782 50 #inst "2026-10-08T06:45:18.977Z" 13194139534782 true] [17592186119514 1100 "Calculate\n$\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}$" 13194139534782 true] [17592186119514 1100 "Calculate\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534782 false] [17592186119514 1145 "The $4$th row of the matrix contains three zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\cdot C_{41} + 0 \\cdot C_{42} + 0 \\cdot C_{43} + (-1) \\cdot C_{44} \\\\\n&= (-1) \\cdot (-1)^{4 + 4} \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= -\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3 \\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix} &= 1 \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}- (-1) \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+ 0 \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= (3 - 8) + (0 - 0) \\\\\n&=-5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" 13194139534782 false] [17592186119514 1145 "The $4$th row of the matrix contains three zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{41}+0\\cdot {C}_{42}+0\\cdot {C}_{43}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3 \\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-8)+(0-0) \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534782 true] [17592186119515 1100 "Using a cofactor expansion along the $2$nd column, write the following determinant as a combination of $3 \\times 3$ determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534782 true] [17592186119515 1100 "Using a cofactor expansion along the $2$nd column, write the following determinant as a combination of $3 \\times 3$ determinants:\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534782 false] [17592186119515 1145 "Using a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} &= 0 \\cdot C_{12} + 3 \\cdot C_{22} + 0 \\cdot C_{32} + 0 \\cdot C_{42} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot (-1)^{2 + 2} \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" 13194139534782 false] [17592186119515 1145 "Using a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{12}+3\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{42} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534782 true] [17592186119584 1100 "Using a cofactor expansion along the $4$th row, write the following determinant as a combination of $3 \\times 3$ determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534782 true] [17592186119584 1100 "Using a cofactor expansion along the $4$th row, write the following determinant as a combination of $3 \\times 3$ determinants:\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534782 false] [17592186119584 1145 "Using a Laplace expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}10 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} &= (-6) \\cdot C_{41} + 0 \\cdot C_{42} + 0 \\cdot C_{43} + 1 \\cdot C_{44} \\\\\n&= (-6) \\cdot (-1)^{4 + 1} \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+ 1 \\cdot (-1)^{4 + 4} \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}10 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= 6 \\cdot\